---
title: Pressure Cooker Mashed Sweet Potatoes
description: Mashed sweet potatoes with butter and cinnamon, cooked under pressure in 15 minutes.
tags: [pressure-cooker]
course: side
source:
  name: "America's Test Kitchen: Pressure Cooker Perfection"
  url: https://www.amazon.com/Pressure-Cooker-Perfection-Americas-Kitchen/dp/1936493411
servings: 4
time: 25m
difficulty: easy
---

> Requires stovetop Pressure Cooker like the [Fagor Duo](http://www.amazon.com/Fagor-8-Quart-Stainless-Steel-Pressure-Steamer/dp/B00023D9RG)

> This recipe can be doubled by increasing time under pressure by 20min

Add the @sweet potatoes{2%lb}(907 g, peeled and sliced 1/2 inch thick), @water{1%cup}(237 ml), and @salt{1/2%tsp} to the #pressure cooker{}. Lock the lid on the pressure cooker.

Put the pressure cooker on the stove over medium-high heat on the high pressure setting.

When the pot reaches high pressure, reduce the heat to medium-low and cook for ~pressure{15%minutes}. Adjust the heat as necessary to maintain pressure.

Remove the pot from the heat and quick release the pressure.

Drain the water from the potatoes using a #colander{}.

Add the @butter{4%tbsp} and @cinnamon{1%tsp} back to the clean and empty pressure cooker pot. Cook on medium heat for ~brown{1-2%minutes} until fragrant.

Add the sweet potatoes back to the pot and mash with a #potato masher{} until they have a uniform and smooth texture.

Fold in the @heavy cream{2%tbsp} and @sugar{3%tbsp}. Season to taste with @&salt{} and @pepper{}.
